Hi,<br><br>library(ggplot2)<br>qplot(class,hwy,data=mpg,geom=&#39;boxplot&#39;)<br><br>I know that boxplot can be plotted in the above way. However, I want to plot boxplot where the mean, sd and 25% and 75% quantiles are available, but the raw data is not. In other word, suppose I only have the &#39;tmp&#39; data.frame as generated below, I want to plot the boxplot using &#39;tmp&#39; only (without plotting the outliers). But I&#39;m not able to find a way to do it with ggplot2. Could anybody kindly let me know how to do it? Thanks!<br>
<br>tmp=do.call(<br>  rbind<br>  , lapply(<br>    with(mpg, split(hwy, class))<br>    , function(x) {<br>      data.frame(<br>        mean=mean(x)<br>        , sd=sd(x)<br>        , quantile25=quantile(x,.25)<br>        , quantile75=quantile(x,.75)<br>
        )<br>    }<br>    )<br>  )<br><br>-- <br>Regards,<br>Peng<br>
